<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd" identifier="pcb-item-96202373bc7c4435b6dfa0b9c906ba85" title="sat-c2-u11-antagonistic.html qc1" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>D</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float"><qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value></qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses antagonistic correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">The relay team&apos;s antagonistic cheering carried their anchor runner to a personal best over the final lap.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">The first storm siren left the whole campground antagonistic for the night, families packing in silence and glancing at the sky.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">The hikers cursed the antagonistic final mile of the trail — loose scree, hairpin switchbacks, and no shade anywhere in the afternoon heat.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">The lighthouse keepers turned antagonistic after the pay dispute, logging complaints against each other and hiding the lamp oil.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Antagonistic means showing active opposition or hostility toward someone or something, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because cheering carries a teammate forward — this is effort spent for someone, the opposite of working against anyone.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Antagonistic means showing active opposition or hostility, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because the campground is frightened of the storm, not set against anybody. Dread has no opponent to push against.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Antagonistic means showing active opposition or hostility, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because a steep trail is merely punishing terrain. Hard going is difficulty, not a stance anyone has taken against the hikers.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Antagonistic means showing active opposition or hostility toward someone or something, and the keepers are working against each other on purpose — complaints logged, lamp oil hidden, opposition put into action on both sides.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
